# v6 (2026-09-12, this repository): every product in products/ was produced by exactly the code fingerprinted in
# CODE_MD5.txt -- the production run tree and this repository were byte-identical for every pipeline file, so
# there is no production/release diff for v6; the diff below is the historical v5 -> release one.
# Changes since v5.2:
#   (d) select_stable.py: the numerical-overflow guard tests the positive side of the log-weight only. A large
#       negative log-weight underflows to zero harmlessly; the two-sided test had rejected sound moment sets on
#       every Sherpa production run (13 TeV max logit 0.9 and 0.3, 13.6 TeV 31 and 6, against a cap of 500).
#   (e) optimizer_DY_unc.py, two changes to the Newton step control. A fit stopped by the step limit with every
#       moment within one sigma of its target counts as converged. The per-event log-weight cap no longer scales
#       the whole step: the Marquardt damping is raised and the step re-solved, with the damping scale floored at
#       1e-6 of the largest Hessian diagonal (a zero or negative diagonal, from signed weights, is then regularised
#       too) and the direction search kept separate from the twelve acceptance attempts. Measured: on 13.6 TeV with
#       20 moments the old control capped 400 of 400 steps at alpha ~ 1e-3 and never reached tolerance; the new one
#       converges. Checked against the earlier products: 13 TeV reproduces its fitted lambdas to 2.7e-7, POWHEG
#       exactly, every validation number to the printed digit. On the current priors the admitted sets contain a
#       direction along which the signed weights cancel; the new control descends it, the prune removes its
#       drivers, and the fit converges on the remainder (15 and 14 moments).
#   (f) add_rate_block.py: 'prior_mean_stored_weight' is no longer written -- it is not a cross section and was
#       read as one. sigma_prior for a Sherpa sample is sum(weights)/sum(trials) from the trials column.
# v5.2 (2026-09-05, this repository): on top of the v5 production code below, the non-convergence remedy of the
# export stage (drop the moment with the largest stationarity residual, re-prune, retry, at most 3 rounds) is also
# applied at the validation stage: run_pipeline.sh (PROG loop) and final_plots_pro.py (fit_lam, strict branch writes
# fullfit_unconverged.json). Found by the fit-sample seed study (13.6 TeV, seed 7). No production run took this path.
# Release provenance: this code is the v5 production pipeline (dyfit/ps, fingerprint CODE_MD5_v5.txt +
# validate_shipped_weights.py) plus the changes made after the production runs. The delivered lambdas
# and per-event weights come from the v5 production code and are NOT affected by any of them.
#   (a) cosmetic, listed in the diff below: three dead local-path fallbacks removed;
#   (b) v5.1, the total-rate block: add_rate_block.py (new), apply_lambdas.py multiplies the weight by
#       the rate factor K (K=1 when the JSON carries none, so the shape is unchanged), run_pipeline.sh
#       step [7/7], verify.py reports the block;
#   (c) v5.2, the validation-stage non-convergence remedy described above (run_pipeline.sh, final_plots_pro.py).
